      "name": "all-purpose flour",
      "amount": "2 1/4 cups",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "unsalted butter, cubed",
      "amount": "1 cup",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "granulated sugar",
      "amount": "1 cup",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "large eggs",
      "amount": "2",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "ground cardamom",
      "amount": "1 tsp",
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "heavy cream",
      "amount": "1/2 cup",
      "notes": "for brushing pastry crust"
    },
    {
      "name": "icing sugar",
      "amount": "1 cup",
      "notes": "for dusting tart"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "preheat oven to 400°f (200°c).",
    "in a large mixing bowl, combine flour, sugar, and cubed butter. Use a pastry blender or your fingers to work butter into flour until mixture resembles coarse crumbs.",
    "add eggs to mixture and stir until dough comes together. Wrap dough in plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.",
    "on a lightly floured surface, roll out chilled dough to a thickness of about 1/8 inch.",
    "transfer dough to a 9-inch tart pan with a removable bottom. Trim edges and press dough into corners of pan."
  ],
